<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h1 id="now" class="doc-h1">Schema-compare PostgreSQL connection</h1>
<p class="doc-muted">Created: 2026-08-26 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Version: 1.1 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Status: ACTIVE (schema branch owns compare; InventoryAccounting owns provision + CoA wizard)</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Now.</strong> PG on .20:5433 accepts a login; schema-compare still dies on Maria SQL (<code>SELECT DATABASE()</code>) after connect. Provision still needs <code>accounting_template</code>. Accounting is opt-in: no books until the SiteName enables the Accounting add-on. Admin card shows only Add until then. Setup step 2 is CREATE DATABASE (tables from template, not the chart). The AI chart wizard is step 3+ on InventoryAccounting and is still a stub.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Next on schema.</strong> Commit this branch when reviewed, merge <em>schema → main from the primary checkout</em> (never <code>git switch main</code> in this worktree), then continue CoA/AI on InventoryAccounting (:4001).</p>
<p class="doc-body">
    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=289">Project #289 SCHEMAPG</a> ·
    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo') %]?project_id=289">Todos</a> ·
    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=5">Parent #5 Schema</a> ·
    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=232">ACCPG #232</a>
</p>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="opt-in" class="doc-h2">Opt-in then setup (owner path)</h2>
<ol class="doc-body">
    <li>Owner adds Accounting on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/membership/addons') %]">/membership/addons</a>. Admin dashboard card is Add-only until that module is enabled for this SiteName (CSC is not auto-opted-in).</li>
    <li>Setup database step = provision <code>&lt;sitename&gt;_accounting</code> from <code>accounting_template</code> (schema tables, not CoA rows). Fails if the template DB is missing. Not an empty database by design.</li>
    <li>Chart wizard (IA :4001) = pick archetype / AI generate into PG <code>Chart</code>. AI route is a stub. Live <code>/Accounting/coa</code> still reads Maria. 3d and BMaster share the template store via <code>site_map.json</code> archetypes, not one chart.</li>
    <li>Existing Maria rows = <code>/Accounting/migrate_to_pg</code> (CoA, GL, suppliers only).</li>
</ol>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="two-systems" class="doc-h2">The two systems (they do not meet)</h2>
<table class="doc-table">
    <thead><tr><th class="doc-th">Piece</th><th class="doc-th">Where</th><th class="doc-th">What it actually does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">Schema-compare</td>
            <td class="doc-td"><code>Controller::Admin::SchemaComparison</code> + <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code> (schema branch)</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Maria Result vs live table. Server cards can <em>label</em> a 5433 port as postgresql, but create/sync uses Ency|Forager, <code>SHOW TABLES</code>, and <code>deployment_statements('MySQL')</code>. <code>$schema-&gt;source</code> is DBEncy.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">RemoteDB</td>
            <td class="doc-td"><code>Model::RemoteDB</code></td>
            <td class="doc-td"><code>get_connection</code> can build <code>dbi:Pg</code>. <code>select_connection</code> skips postgresql as Invalid db_type (allowlist mysql|sqlite|mariadb ~line 403). Compare never gets a PG handle through the selector.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">PG provision</td>
            <td class="doc-td"><code>Model::AccountingDB::provision_site</code> (InventoryAccounting)</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Admin connect to maintenance DB <code>postgres</code>, then <code>CREATE DATABASE "&lt;site&gt;_accounting" TEMPLATE accounting_template</code>. Refuses if <code>accounting_template</code> is missing. Not called from schema-compare.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">PG Result tree</td>
            <td class="doc-td"><code>Model::Schema::Accounting::Result::*</code> (~25 LedgerSMB-shaped classes)</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Clone-target ORM. No live per-site PG DBs yet. Different namespace from <code>Ency::Result::Accounting::*</code> (Maria live CoA/inventory).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">Secrets</td>
            <td class="doc-td"><code>~/.comserv/secrets/dbi/db_production_postgres.json</code></td>
            <td class="doc-td">Shape only: host 192.168.1.20, port 5433, database=csc, db_type=postgresql, server_group=db-server-1, role=primary. Dev file points at .198:5432 (TCP refused 2026-08-26).</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p class="doc-info">The 2026-08-26 <code>Can't find source for Accounting::InventoryPurchaseOrderLine</code> error was the <strong>Maria</strong> path: <code>Ency::Result::Accounting::InventoryPurchaseOrderLine</code> on InventoryAccounting :4001. That server had been up since 22 Aug; the Result files landed 26 Aug 20:36, so DBEncy never registered the source. That is not this PG plan — see <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2332">#2332</a>.</p>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="measured" class="doc-h2">Measured 2026-08-26 (perishable)</h2>
<ul class="doc-body">
    <li>TCP 192.168.1.20:5433 OPEN; 192.168.1.20:5432 OPEN; 192.168.1.198:5432 refused. No postgres listener on the workstation itself.</li>
    <li><code>accounting_template.sql</code> exists in both schema and InventoryAccounting trees. Existence of the <em>database</em> <code>accounting_template</code> on .20 was not queried (would need a PG login). <code>provision_site</code> will fail until that DB exists.</li>
    <li>Schema-compare create is Maria-only (SchemaComparison.pm ~848–904).</li>
    <li>Hand-running <code>sql/accounting_template.sql</code> is forbidden (Result class is source of truth).</li>
</ul>
<p class="doc-warning">Re-probe before coding. These readings are not current fact a week later.</p>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 id="tracking" class="doc-h2">Project tracking</h2>
<p class="doc-body">Parent project <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=5">#5 Schema</a>. This plan is <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=289">#289 SCHEMAPG</a>. Named sub-projects (not “Phase N”). GATE = done-when.</p>
<table class="doc-table">
    <thead><tr><th class="doc-th">Sub-project</th><th class="doc-th">Todo</th><th class="doc-th">Gate</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=290">#290 SCPG-EVAL</a></td>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2323">#2323</a> role eval · <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2324">#2324</a> dep check</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Evidence in the todo body; re-measure before the next sub-project.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=291">#291 SCPG-REMOTEDB</a></td>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2325">#2325</a> allowlist (blocks others) · <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2326">#2326</a> named get_connection</td>
            <td class="doc-td">A named PG secret connects or returns the real Pg error — never Invalid db_type.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=292">#292 SCPG-COMPARE</a></td>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2327">#2327</a> list PG DBs · <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2328">#2328</a> Accounting namespace</td>
            <td class="doc-td">PG card lists PG databases; Create Table on a PG Result does not run SHOW TABLES.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=293">#293 SCPG-CREATEDB</a></td>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2329">#2329</a> first DB from compare · <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2330">#2330</a> provision_site (IA)</td>
            <td class="doc-td">A PG database exists that compare created. No hand SQL. D1 decided first.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=294">#294 SCPG-DEPLOY</a></td>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2331">#2331</a> one Result · <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2332">#2332</a> PO engine decision</td>
            <td class="doc-td">One PG table matches its Result. D2 recorded before any InventoryPurchaseOrder create.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">#289 parent</td>
            <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2333">#2333</a> ROUTINE re-audit</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Plan META/TOC/ids still true; PG probe refreshed.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p class="doc-muted">Branch split: #2325–2328, #2331 schema worktree. #2330 InventoryAccounting. #2329 needs both after D1.</p>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
